{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EV3LycfCQWguJQF3fRJ27A","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Context window h-sweep ablation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Sweep h={1,2,3,5,8,10,15,20,full} on same GRPO config. Paper核心Figure。\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"h1_success_rate\": 0.0,\n7\t      \"h2_success_rate\": 2.0,\n8\t      \"h3_success_rate\": 4.5,\n9\t      \"h5_success_rate\": 8.0,\n10\t      \"h8_success_rate\": 14.0,\n11\t      \"h10_success_rate\": 18.0,\n12\t      \"h15_success_rate\": 22.0,\n13\t      \"h20_success_rate\": 24.0,\n14\t      \"h_full_success_rate\": 25.0,\n15\t      \"cliff_threshold_h\": 5,\n16\t      \"h1_collapse_rate\": 1.0,\n17\t      \"h2_collapse_rate\": 0.85,\n18\t      \"h5_action_is_valid\": 72.0,\n19\t      \"h10_action_is_valid\": 82.0,\n20\t      \"h_full_action_is_valid\": 88.0,\n21\t      \"convergence_speed_h10_steps\": 15,\n22\t      \"convergence_speed_h_full_steps\": 8\n23\t    },\n24\t    \"tables\": [\n25\t      {\n26\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: h-sweep results\",\n27\t        \"columns\": [\n28\t          \"h\",\n29\t          \"success_rate(%)\",\n30\t          \"action_is_valid(%)\",\n31\t          \"convergence_step\",\n32\t          \"effective_discount_gamma^(T-h)_mean\"\n33\t        ],\n34\t        \"rows\": [\n35\t          [\n36\t            1,\n37\t            0.0,\n38\t            45.0,\n39\t            \"N/A (collapse)\",\n40\t            0.0001\n41\t          ],\n42\t          [\n43\t            2,\n44\t            2.0,\n45\t            58.0,\n46\t            \"N/A (near-collapse)\",\n47\t            0.0008\n48\t          ],\n49\t          [\n50\t            3,\n51\t            4.5,\n52\t            65.0,\n53\t            20,\n54\t            0.005\n55\t          ],\n56\t          [\n57\t            5,\n58\t            8.0,\n59\t            72.0,\n60\t            15,\n61\t            0.03\n62\t          ],\n63\t          [\n64\t            8,\n65\t            14.0,\n66\t            79.0,\n67\t            12,\n68\t            0.12\n69\t          ],\n70\t          [\n71\t            10,\n72\t            18.0,\n73\t            82.0,\n74\t            12,\n75\t            0.22\n76\t          ],\n77\t          [\n78\t            15,\n79\t            22.0,\n80\t            85.0,\n81\t            10,\n82\t            0.48\n83\t          ],\n84\t          [\n85\t            20,\n86\t            24.0,\n87\t            87.0,\n88\t            8,\n89\t            0.67\n90\t          ],\n91\t          [\n92\t            \"full\",\n93\t            25.0,\n94\t            88.0,\n95\t            8,\n96\t            1.0\n97\t          ]\n98\t        ]\n99\t      }\n100\t    ],\n101\t    \"figures\": [],\n102\t    \"analysis\": \"h-sweep是worst档下paper最有价值的contribution。虽然绝对性能低，但趋势清晰：step-independent（h=1-2）catastrophically fails，episode-level（h=full）works。问题在于h=10已达full性能的72%（18/25），reviewer会argue full episode context非必要。Defense需要：(1)强调h=10在更长episode task上可能不够，(2)展示h=full的convergence speed优势，(3)argue 'full是最简方案，无需tune h'。Single seed数据使得intermediate h values的ordering可能有noise。\\n\\n在worst档位下，h-sweep仍能展示episode-level vs step-independent的gap，但曲线形态偏向gradual degradation而非sharp cliff。h=5以下gamma^(T-h)衰减到<1%导致几乎无学习信号，但h=10到h=full之间差距不大（18%→25%），削弱了'episode-level is critical'的论证力度——reviewer会argue h=10 already sufficient。绝对性能ceiling在25%使得整条曲线都不impressive。cliff在h=5左右，比hypothesis的h=10低，意味着credit assignment threshold比预期更宽松，但也说明即便给了足够context（h≥10），1.7B model的能力ceiling也只有20-25%。\"\n103\t  },\n104\t  {\n105\t    \"name\": \"Multi-seed replication (3 seeds)\",\n106\t    \"description\": \"2 additional seeds for episode-level config. Report mean ± std。\",\n107\t    \"results\": {\n108\t      \"seed1_success_rate\": 25.0,\n109\t      \"seed2_success_rate\": 18.0,\n110\t      \"seed3_success_rate\": 30.0,\n111\t      \"mean_success_rate\": 24.3,\n112\t      \"std_success_rate\": 6.0,\n113\t      \"seed1_convergence_step\": 8,\n114\t      \"seed2_convergence_step\": 15,\n115\t      \"seed3_convergence_step\": 6,\n116\t      \"seed1_action_is_valid\": 88.0,\n117\t      \"seed2_action_is_valid\": 82.0,\n118\t      \"seed3_action_is_valid\": 90.0,\n119\t      \"mean_action_is_valid\": 86.7,\n120\t      \"std_action_is_valid\": 4.2\n121\t    },\n122\t    \"tables\": [\n123\t      {\n124\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Multi-seed episode-level results\",\n125\t        \"columns\": [\n126\t          \"Seed\",\n127\t          \"Success Rate(%)\",\n128\t          \"Action Valid(%)\",\n129\t          \"Convergence Step\",\n130\t          \"Final KL\"\n131\t        ],\n132\t        \"rows\": [\n133\t          [\n134\t            42,\n135\t            25.0,\n136\t            88.0,\n137\t            8,\n138\t            0.048\n139\t          ],\n140\t          [\n141\t            123,\n142\t            18.0,\n143\t            82.0,\n144\t            15,\n145\t            0.092\n146\t          ],\n147\t          [\n148\t            7,\n149\t            30.0,\n150\t            90.0,\n151\t            6,\n152\t            0.035\n153\t          ],\n154\t          [\n155\t            \"Mean±Std\",\n156\t            \"24.3±6.0\",\n157\t            \"86.7±4.2\",\n158\t            \"9.7±4.7\",\n159\t            \"0.058±0.030\"\n160\t          ]\n161\t        ]\n162\t      }\n163\t    ],\n164\t    \"figures\": [],\n165\t    \"analysis\": \"Std=6pp略好于worst档定义的8-12pp下界，但仍然problematic。N=3 seeds给出的confidence interval很宽（24.3±6.0意味着95% CI约为[12, 37]），reviewer会正确指出这不够。理想需要5+ seeds但GPU budget不允许。Defense策略：(1)承认limitation，(2)强调所有seeds都远超step-independent baseline 0%，(3)variance主要在收敛speed而非final direction。\\n\\nWorst档定义multi-seed std>8pp，但我预测实际std在6-9pp范围——足以让reviewer质疑但不至于完全破坏结论。三个seed中一个会表现较差（18%），一个中等（25%，复现原始结果），一个稍好（30%）。这个variance部分来自ALFWorld task sampling的随机性（val set只有16 episodes），部分来自GRPO的inherent instability（高grad_norm, KL spikes在不同seed上timing不同）。1.7B模型的parameter space小，不同random init导致loss landscape上收敛到不同local optima。Mean 24.3%仍远超step-independent baseline（0-6%），但confidence interval宽。\"\n166\t  },\n167\t  {\n168\t    \"name\": \"Credit assignment mechanism analysis (paper Figure 2)\",\n169\t    \"description\": \"计算并可视化gamma^(T-h) effective discount, gradient signal strength, episode length correlation。\",\n170\t    \"results\": {\n171\t      \"gamma_value_used\": 0.99,\n172\t      \"mean_episode_length_T\": 48,\n173\t      \"gamma_T_minus_1\": 0.0061,\n174\t      \"gamma_T_minus_2\": 0.0062,\n175\t      \"gamma_T_minus_5\": 0.0065,\n176\t      \"gamma_T_minus_10\": 0.0068,\n177\t      \"gamma_T_minus_20\": 0.0075,\n178\t      \"gamma_T_minus_full\": 1.0,\n179\t      \"gradient_signal_h1_relative\": 0.006,\n180\t      \"gradient_signal_h5_relative\": 0.03,\n181\t      \"gradient_signal_h10_relative\": 0.22,\n182\t      \"gradient_signal_full_relative\": 1.0,\n183\t      \"episode_length_success_correlation\": -0.35,\n184\t      \"long_episode_success_drop_under_h5\": 95\n185\t    },\n186\t    \"tables\": [\n187\t      {\n188\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Effective discount factor analysis\",\n189\t        \"columns\": [\n190\t          \"h\",\n191\t          \"Mean gamma^(T-h)\",\n192\t          \"Relative Gradient Signal\",\n193\t          \"Observed Success(%)\"\n194\t        ],\n195\t        \"rows\": [\n196\t          [\n197\t            1,\n198\t            0.006,\n199\t            \"0.6%\",\n200\t            0.0\n201\t          ],\n202\t          [\n203\t            2,\n204\t            0.012,\n205\t            \"1.2%\",\n206\t            2.0\n207\t          ],\n208\t          [\n209\t            5,\n210\t            0.03,\n211\t            \"3.0%\",\n212\t            8.0\n213\t          ],\n214\t          [\n215\t            10,\n216\t            0.22,\n217\t            \"22%\",\n218\t            18.0\n219\t          ],\n220\t          [\n221\t            20,\n222\t            0.67,\n223\t            \"67%\",\n224\t            24.0\n225\t          ],\n226\t          [\n227\t            \"full\",\n228\t            1.0,\n229\t            \"100%\",\n230\t            25.0\n231\t          ]\n232\t        ]\n233\t      }\n234\t    ],\n235\t    \"figures\": [],\n236\t    \"analysis\": \"这是worst档下最强的contribution piece。数学关系清晰，可视化compelling。关键insight：在RAGEN等现有工作中，默认h=1（step-independent），对应gradient signal仅0.6%——解释了为什么这些方法在long-horizon tasks上struggle。但需要小心措辞：不能overclaim 'episode-level solves multi-turn RL'（因为25%不算solved），只能claim 'episode-level is necessary first step, removing a fundamental training bottleneck'。\\n\\nMechanistic analysis本身是deterministic计算（给定gamma和episode length分布），不受worst档位的performance ceiling影响。ALFWorld平均episode length~48 steps，所以gamma^47≈0.006（h=1时first action的discount）。这个数学事实不变。但worst档下的complication是：即使h=full（gradient signal=1.0），模型也只达25%——说明gradient signal是necessary但非sufficient condition。Reviewer会argue：'你解决了gradient signal问题，但模型仍然不行，说明bottleneck在elsewhere'。需要explicitly address这一点：承认model capacity是另一个bottleneck，但credit assignment是第一个需解决的。\"\n237\t  },\n238\t  {\n239\t    \"name\": \"Action-change statistics from always-on runs\",\n240\t    \"description\": \"从exp029 checkpoints收集action-change统计：confirmatory rate, correlation with success, per-task breakdown。\",\n241\t    \"results\": {\n242\t      \"total_verification_episodes\": 48,\n243\t      \"action_change_rate\": 0.35,\n244\t      \"confirmatory_rate\": 0.65,\n245\t      \"action_change_success_correlation_r\": 0.15,\n246\t      \"action_change_success_correlation_p\": 0.18,\n247\t      \"per_task_confirmatory_rate_put\": 0.72,\n248\t      \"per_task_confirmatory_rate_clean\": 0.6,\n249\t      \"per_task_confirmatory_rate_heat\": 0.55,\n250\t      \"per_task_confirmatory_rate_cool\": 0.58,\n251\t      \"per_task_confirmatory_rate_examine\": 0.7,\n252\t      \"action_change_leads_to_success_rate\": 0.22,\n253\t      \"no_change_leads_to_success_rate\": 0.18\n254\t    },\n255\t    \"tables\": [\n256\t      {\n257\t        \"name\": \"Table: Action-change statistics\",\n258\t        \"columns\": [\n259\t          \"Metric\",\n260\t          \"Value\",\n261\t          \"95% CI\"\n262\t        ],\n263\t        \"rows\": [\n264\t          [\n265\t            \"Confirmatory rate (no action change)\",\n266\t            \"65%\",\n267\t            \"[52%, 78%]\"\n268\t          ],\n269\t          [\n270\t            \"Action change rate\",\n271\t            \"35%\",\n272\t            \"[22%, 48%]\"\n273\t          ],\n274\t          [\n275\t            \"Correlation (action_change, success)\",\n276\t            \"r=0.15\",\n277\t            \"p=0.18\"\n278\t          ],\n279\t          [\n280\t            \"Success | action_change\",\n281\t            \"22%\",\n282\t            \"[10%, 34%]\"\n283\t          ],\n284\t          [\n285\t            \"Success | no_change\",\n286\t            \"18%\",\n287\t            \"[8%, 28%]\"\n288\t          ]\n289\t        ]\n290\t      }\n291\t    ],\n292\t    \"figures\": [],\n293\t    \"analysis\": \"统计结果不支持action-change作为meaningful reward signal。Correlation not significant，delta too small，CI too wide。这组数据是worst档叙事转向的empirical justification：不是我们选择不做selective verification，而是数据显示在当前performance level下selective verification lacks statistical grounding。Paper中可以brief mention作为'future work when base agent is stronger'。\\n\\n在worst档下，episode-level model只有25% success rate，导致action-change统计的样本量极小且noisy。Confirmatory rate 65%落在worst档定义的50-70%范围内，但correlation with success仅r=0.15（p=0.18, not significant）。这是因为：(1)成功episodes太少（~12/48），统计power不足；(2)25%的模型经常在错误轨道上，verification后的action change可能是从一个错误action换到另一个错误action，而非corrective。Action change→success rate (22%) vs no change→success rate (18%)的delta仅4pp，远不够支撑'action change is informative signal'的claim。这直接explains为什么在worst档下必须放弃selective verification story。\"\n294\t  },\n295\t  {\n296\t    \"name\": \"Selective verification implementation\",\n297\t    \"description\": \"实现binary verify/skip decision。Code-only, no GPU。\",\n298\t    \"results\": {\n299\t      \"implementation_status\": \"completed\",\n300\t      \"code_lines_added\": 350,\n301\t      \"integration_test_pass\": true,\n302\t      \"note\": \"implementation ready but not deployed for training due to plan_005 results\"\n303\t    },\n304\t    \"tables\": [],\n305\t    \"figures\": [],\n306\t    \"analysis\": \"在worst档叙事下，这个实验stop at implementation。Paper中不报告selective verification training results，而是在discussion section brief mention implementation exists but 'requires stronger base agent to provide meaningful training signal'。\\n\\nImplementation本身是engineering work，不受worst档影响。代码可以完成，但基于plan_005的统计结果（action-change correlation not significant），decision是不proceed to training。代码保留为future work artifact。\"\n307\t  },\n308\t  {\n309\t    \"name\": \"B-IAVR selective verification training\",\n310\t    \"description\": \"Train selective verification policy via episode-level GRPO。在worst档下执行但预期效果不佳。\",\n311\t    \"results\": {\n312\t      \"training_status\": \"completed_but_ineffective\",\n313\t      \"final_success_rate\": 18.0,\n314\t      \"always_on_baseline_success\": 25.0,\n315\t      \"success_delta_vs_always_on\": -7.0,\n316\t      \"verification_rate_reduction\": 12.0,\n317\t      \"cost_reduction_pct\": 8.0,\n318\t      \"training_stability\": \"unstable\",\n319\t      \"convergence_step\": \"no clear convergence\",\n320\t      \"reward_signal_noise\": \"high\"\n321\t    },\n322\t    \"tables\": [\n323\t      {\n324\t        \"name\": \"Table: B-IAVR training outcome\",\n325\t        \"columns\": [\n326\t          \"Config\",\n327\t          \"Success(%)\",\n328\t          \"Verify Rate(%)\",\n329\t          \"Cost Reduction(%)\"\n330\t        ],\n331\t        \"rows\": [\n332\t          [\n333\t            \"Always-on (baseline)\",\n334\t            25.0,\n335\t            100,\n336\t            0\n337\t          ],\n338\t          [\n339\t            \"B-IAVR (trained)\",\n340\t            18.0,\n341\t            88,\n342\t            8\n343\t          ],\n344\t          [\n345\t            \"Delta\",\n346\t            -7.0,\n347\t            -12,\n348\t            \"+8\"\n349\t          ]\n350\t        ]\n351\t      }\n352\t    ],\n353\t    \"figures\": [],\n354\t    \"analysis\": \"结果confirms worst档prediction：selective verification在base agent只有25%时无法有意义地训练。-7pp success drop换取仅8% cost reduction，Pareto-dominated by always-on。Paper中不报告此结果，或仅作为negative result brief mention to motivate 'stronger base agent needed'。\\n\\nWorst档定义selective_verification_rate_reduction在0-15%，selective_vs_always_on_success_delta在8-15pp。模型从25% base开始，加入verify/skip decision后引入额外exploration space，但base performance本身就marginal。Agent在只有25% success的情况下，缺乏足够的positive reward signal来学习WHEN to verify——大部分trajectory都是failure，无论verify还是skip。结果是verification rate仅下降12%（几乎always verify因为policy没学到有用的skip pattern），且success下降7pp（从25%到18%）因为额外decision point增加了policy complexity。这不构成meaningful contribution。\"\n355\t  },\n356\t  {\n357\t    \"name\": \"Selective verification full comparison\",\n358\t    \"description\": \"Compare always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold。\",\n359\t    \"results\": {\n360\t      \"always_on_success\": 25.0,\n361\t      \"always_on_verify_rate\": 100,\n362\t      \"biavr_success\": 18.0,\n363\t      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 88,\n364\t      \"no_verify_success\": 15.0,\n365\t      \"no_verify_verify_rate\": 0,\n366\t      \"random_p50_success\": 20.0,\n367\t      \"random_p50_verify_rate\": 50,\n368\t      \"confidence_threshold_success\": 21.0,\n369\t      \"confidence_threshold_verify_rate\": 65\n370\t    },\n371\t    \"tables\": [\n372\t      {\n373\t        \"name\": \"Table: Full comparison (NOT included in worst-tier paper)\",\n374\t        \"columns\": [\n375\t          \"Method\",\n376\t          \"Success(%)\",\n377\t          \"Verify Rate(%)\",\n378\t          \"Tokens/Episode\",\n379\t          \"Cost Reduction(%)\"\n380\t        ],\n381\t        \"rows\": [\n382\t          [\n383\t            \"Always-on\",\n384\t            25.0,\n385\t            100,\n386\t            4800,\n387\t            0\n388\t          ],\n389\t          [\n390\t            \"B-IAVR (ours)\",\n391\t            18.0,\n392\t            88,\n393\t            4420,\n394\t            8\n395\t          ],\n396\t          [\n397\t            \"No-verify\",\n398\t            15.0,\n399\t            0,\n400\t            2400,\n401\t            50\n402\t          ],\n403\t          [\n404\t            \"Random-p=0.5\",\n405\t            20.0,\n406\t            50,\n407\t            3600,\n408\t            25\n409\t          ],\n410\t          [\n411\t            \"Confidence-threshold\",\n412\t            21.0,\n413\t            65,\n414\t            3900,\n415\t            19\n416\t          ]\n417\t        ]\n418\t      }\n419\t    ],\n420\t    \"figures\": [],\n421\t    \"analysis\": \"This entire comparison suite becomes 'data we collected but don't include in paper'。B-IAVR被simpler baselines dominate是fatal for selective verification claim。在worst档pure methodology paper中，这组数据的唯一价值是supporting the narrative 'future work: once episode-level training achieves higher ceiling, selective verification becomes viable'。\\n\\n在25% ceiling下，所有selective methods都worse than always-on。Random-p=0.5 (20%) actually competitive with trained B-IAVR (18%)——trained policy没有学到比random更好的策略，这是devastating negative result。Confidence-threshold (21%) slightly better因为它是heuristic rule而非learned，less prone to policy degradation。整个comparison suite展示：在low-performance regime下，verification的选择性本身不是bottleneck，base capability才是。\"\n422\t  },\n423\t  {\n424\t    \"name\": \"No-verify ablation\",\n425\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level GRPO without self-verification。Lower bound实验。\",\n426\t    \"results\": {\n427\t      \"success_rate\": 15.0,\n428\t      \"action_is_valid\": 78.0,\n429\t      \"delta_vs_always_on\": -10.0,\n430\t      \"mean_episode_length\": 38,\n431\t      \"convergence_step\": 10\n432\t    },\n433\t    \"tables\": [\n434\t      {\n435\t        \"name\": \"Table: Verification value\",\n436\t        \"columns\": [\n437\t          \"Config\",\n438\t          \"Success(%)\",\n439\t          \"Action Valid(%)\",\n440\t          \"Avg Steps\"\n441\t        ],\n442\t        \"rows\": [\n443\t          [\n444\t            \"Episode-level + verification\",\n445\t            25.0,\n446\t            88.0,\n447\t            48\n448\t          ],\n449\t          [\n450\t            \"Episode-level, no verification\",\n451\t            15.0,\n452\t            78.0,\n453\t            38\n454\t          ],\n455\t          [\n456\t            \"Step-independent + verification\",\n457\t            0.0,\n458\t            65.0,\n459\t            50\n460\t          ]\n461\t        ]\n462\t      }\n463\t    ],\n464\t    \"figures\": [],\n465\t    \"analysis\": \"三行对比table实际很有说服力：step-independent完全fails无论有无verification，episode-level without verification仍有15%。Message: training methodology是前提条件，verification是锦上添花。这fit worst档pure methodology paper的narrative。\\n\\n移除verification后，agent失去每步的self-correction机会。从25%降到15%，delta=10pp。这在worst档下actually是有用的数据点——证明verification本身有10pp价值。但这个delta不够dramatic来支撑'selective verification is the key innovation'的story。在pure methodology paper中可以brief report作为：'verification contributes +10pp, confirming its utility, but our focus is on the training methodology that enables ANY multi-turn RL to work'。\"\n466\t  },\n467\t  {\n468\t    \"name\": \"Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\",\n469\t    \"description\": \"Stratify action-change correlation by policy entropy, test partial correlation。\",\n470\t    \"results\": {\n471\t      \"overall_correlation_r\": 0.15,\n472\t      \"overall_p\": 0.18,\n473\t      \"low_entropy_stratum_r\": 0.08,\n474\t      \"low_entropy_stratum_p\": 0.55,\n475\t      \"high_entropy_stratum_r\": 0.2,\n476\t      \"high_entropy_stratum_p\": 0.22,\n477\t      \"partial_correlation_controlling_entropy\": 0.12,\n478\t      \"partial_correlation_p\": 0.28,\n479\t      \"n_episodes_per_stratum\": 24\n480\t    },\n481\t    \"tables\": [],\n482\t    \"figures\": [],\n483\t    \"analysis\": \"在worst档下这组分析的结论是negative：无法reject null hypothesis (action-change = noise)。Paper中不report，或在appendix作为'limitation: at current performance level, insufficient statistical power to establish action-change as reliable signal'。\\n\\n在worst档25% success下，整体correlation已not significant (r=0.15, p=0.18)。Stratify by entropy后每层只有~24 episodes，statistical power进一步削弱。Low entropy stratum（policy confident）中action-change很少发生（agent已committed to action），correlation near zero。High entropy stratum中有more action-change但也more randomness，correlation略高但仍not significant。Partial correlation r=0.12 (p=0.28)完全不支持'action-change is signal not noise'的claim。根本原因：样本量太小 + base performance太低导致signal-to-noise ratio极差。\"\n484\t  },\n485\t  {\n486\t    \"name\": \"Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes\",\n487\t    \"description\": \"Inject random action changes vs verification-triggered. Compare success。\",\n488\t    \"results\": {\n489\t      \"verification_triggered_success\": 22.0,\n490\t      \"random_change_success\": 16.0,\n491\t      \"no_change_baseline_success\": 18.0,\n492\t      \"delta_triggered_vs_random\": 6.0,\n493\t      \"delta_triggered_vs_random_p\": 0.25,\n494\t      \"n_episodes\": 48\n495\t    },\n496\t    \"tables\": [\n497\t      {\n498\t        \"name\": \"Table: Causal intervention (insufficient power)\",\n499\t        \"columns\": [\n500\t          \"Condition\",\n501\t          \"Success(%)\",\n502\t          \"N\",\n503\t          \"95% CI\"\n504\t        ],\n505\t        \"rows\": [\n506\t          [\n507\t            \"Verification-triggered change\",\n508\t            22.0,\n509\t            48,\n510\t            \"[11%, 33%]\"\n511\t          ],\n512\t          [\n513\t            \"Random change (same rate)\",\n514\t            16.0,\n515\t            48,\n516\t            \"[6%, 26%]\"\n517\t          ],\n518\t          [\n519\t            \"No change control\",\n520\t            18.0,\n521\t            48,\n522\t            \"[8%, 28%]\"\n523\t          ]\n524\t        ]\n525\t      }\n526\t    ],\n527\t    \"figures\": [],\n528\t    \"analysis\": \"CIs完全overlap。Experiment was run but results inconclusive。在pure methodology paper中不report。File under 'more data needed at higher performance level'。\\n\\nVerification-triggered changes (22%) vs random changes (16%) shows 6pp gap，方向正确但p=0.25 not significant。N=48 episodes不够detect这个effect size。No-change baseline (18%)介于两者之间，使得interpretation模糊：triggered changes可能beneficial，但也可能just noise given wide CIs。在25% performance regime下，即使verification IS informative，effect size太小to detect reliably。另一个confounder：random changes有时accidentally correct（16% vs no-change 18%只差2pp），suggesting verification的causal contribution marginal。\"\n529\t  },\n530\t  {\n531\t    \"name\": \"Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\",\n532\t    \"description\": \"Train B-IAVR with different reward signals: action-change, random, confidence-based。\",\n533\t    \"results\": {\n534\t      \"action_change_reward_success\": 18.0,\n535\t      \"action_change_reward_verify_rate\": 88,\n536\t      \"random_reward_success\": 17.0,\n537\t      \"random_reward_verify_rate\": 82,\n538\t      \"confidence_reward_success\": 19.0,\n539\t      \"confidence_reward_verify_rate\": 85,\n540\t      \"all_configs_worse_than_always_on\": true,\n541\t      \"best_reward_signal\": \"confidence (marginal)\"\n542\t    },\n543\t    \"tables\": [\n544\t      {\n545\t        \"name\": \"Table: Reward ablation (NOT in paper)\",\n546\t        \"columns\": [\n547\t          \"Reward Signal\",\n548\t          \"Success(%)\",\n549\t          \"Verify Rate(%)\",\n550\t          \"vs Always-on Delta\"\n551\t        ],\n552\t        \"rows\": [\n553\t          [\n554\t            \"Action-change (ours)\",\n555\t            18.0,\n556\t            88,\n557\t            -7\n558\t          ],\n559\t          [\n560\t            \"Random trigger\",\n561\t            17.0,\n562\t            82,\n563\t            -8\n564\t          ],\n565\t          [\n566\t            \"Confidence-based\",\n567\t            19.0,\n568\t            85,\n569\t            -6\n570\t          ],\n571\t          [\n572\t            \"Always-on (no selection)\",\n573\t            25.0,\n574\t            100,\n575\t            0\n576\t          ]\n577\t        ]\n578\t      }\n579\t    ],\n580\t    \"figures\": [],\n581\t    \"analysis\": \"192 GPU hours for a negative result。在worst档下，建议NOT run此实验——plan_007的negative result已sufficient to abandon selective verification direction。Save GPU budget for more h-sweep seeds or ScienceWorld transfer。\\n\\n所有reward signals在25% base下都无法学到meaningful selective policy。Action-change reward (18%, verify 88%) vs random reward (17%, verify 82%)的差距仅1pp success——action-change没有demonstrable advantage over random。Confidence-based reward margionally better (19%) because它at least correlates with model's own uncertainty（哪怕calibration差）。但关键point：所有trained selective policies都worse than always-on (25%)。Reward signal choice irrelevant when base performance insufficient to generate learning signal。192 GPU hours换来的结论是'all approaches fail equally in low-performance regime'。\"\n582\t  },\n583\t  {\n584\t    \"name\": \"ARES reproduction + comparison\",\n585\t    \"description\": \"Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR。\",\n586\t    \"results\": {\n587\t      \"ares_success\": 20.0,\n588\t      \"ares_verify_rate\": 60,\n589\t      \"ares_cost_reduction\": 30,\n590\t      \"biavr_success\": 18.0,\n591\t      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 88,\n592\t      \"biavr_cost_reduction\": 8,\n593\t      \"ares_dominates_biavr\": true\n594\t    },\n595\t    \"tables\": [\n596\t      {\n597\t        \"name\": \"Table: ARES comparison (NOT in paper)\",\n598\t        \"columns\": [\n599\t          \"Method\",\n600\t          \"Success(%)\",\n601\t          \"Verify Rate(%)\",\n602\t          \"Cost Red.(%)\"\n603\t        ],\n604\t        \"rows\": [\n605\t          [\n606\t            \"Always-on\",\n607\t            25.0,\n608\t            100,\n609\t            0\n610\t          ],\n611\t          [\n612\t            \"ARES (SFT router)\",\n613\t            20.0,\n614\t            60,\n615\t            30\n616\t          ],\n617\t          [\n618\t            \"B-IAVR (ours, RL)\",\n619\t            18.0,\n620\t            88,\n621\t            8\n622\t          ]\n623\t        ]\n624\t      }\n625\t    ],\n626\t    \"figures\": [],\n627\t    \"analysis\": \"ARES dominates B-IAVR on Pareto frontier。但在worst档pure methodology paper中，这个comparison不needed也不helpful。如果include，只会invite reviewer质疑'why not just use SFT'。建议NOT run，节省24 GPU hours。\\n\\nARES使用SFT（supervised从expert demonstrations学）which is more data-efficient than RL in low-performance regime。SFT router可以直接学human-pattern的'when to verify'而不依赖agent自身的exploration。预测ARES achieves 20% success at 60% verify rate，Pareto-dominating B-IAVR (18% at 88% verify rate)。这是because SFT不需要agent自己产生positive signal——它从expert data中学。Devastating for our RL-based approach，但irrelevant for worst档paper because we abandon selective verification entirely。\"\n628\t  },\n629\t  {\n630\t    \"name\": \"ScienceWorld transfer (episode-level advantage)\",\n631\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld。Second environment for generalization。\",\n632\t    \"results\": {\n633\t      \"episode_level_success\": 15.0,\n634\t      \"step_independent_success\": 2.0,\n635\t      \"episode_level_action_is_valid\": 75.0,\n636\t      \"step_independent_action_is_valid\": 55.0,\n637\t      \"episode_level_convergence_step\": 12,\n638\t      \"step_independent_collapse_step\": 4,\n639\t      \"mean_episode_length_scienceworld\": 35\n640\t    },\n641\t    \"tables\": [\n642\t      {\n643\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-environment validation\",\n644\t        \"columns\": [\n645\t          \"Environment\",\n646\t          \"Episode-Level(%)\",\n647\t          \"Step-Independent(%)\",\n648\t          \"Ratio\",\n649\t          \"Mean Episode Length\"\n650\t        ],\n651\t        \"rows\": [\n652\t          [\n653\t            \"ALFWorld\",\n654\t            25.0,\n655\t            0.0,\n656\t            \"∞ (0→25)\",\n657\t            48\n658\t          ],\n659\t          [\n660\t            \"ScienceWorld\",\n661\t            15.0,\n662\t            2.0,\n663\t            \"7.5x\",\n664\t            35\n665\t          ]\n666\t        ]\n667\t      }\n668\t    ],\n669\t    \"figures\": [],\n670\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-environment result是worst档paper的第二大contribution。Pattern consistent across environments strongly支持mechanistic explanation。Reviewer concern #2 (single env) addressed。72 GPU hours well-spent for worst档narrative。绝对值低但ratio large，且collapse pattern identical——这是methodology insight的generalization evidence。\\n\\nScienceWorld比ALFWorld更难（state space更大，natural language更复杂），1.7B model的absolute performance会更低。Episode-level仍展示优势（15% vs 2%），倍率~7.5x（高于ALFWorld的~4x因为ScienceWorld的longer episodes使credit assignment问题更severe）。Step-independent在step 4 collapse（与ALFWorld pattern一致）。绝对数字15%不impressive，但cross-environment consistency是powerful evidence for the mechanism。在worst档pure methodology paper中，这是ADDRESS single-environment concern的关键实验。\"\n671\t  },\n672\t  {\n673\t    \"name\": \"7B model scaling verification\",\n674\t    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B。Address model size concern。\",\n675\t    \"results\": {\n676\t      \"episode_level_7b_success\": 38.0,\n677\t      \"step_independent_7b_success\": 5.0,\n678\t      \"episode_level_7b_action_is_valid\": 92.0,\n679\t      \"step_independent_7b_collapse_step\": 5,\n680\t      \"episode_level_7b_convergence_step\": 6,\n681\t      \"delta_7b_vs_1_7b_episode_level\": 13\n682\t    },\n683\t    \"tables\": [\n684\t      {\n685\t        \"name\": \"Table: Model scaling\",\n686\t        \"columns\": [\n687\t          \"Model\",\n688\t          \"Episode-Level(%)\",\n689\t          \"Step-Independent(%)\",\n690\t          \"Advantage\"\n691\t        ],\n692\t        \"rows\": [\n693\t          [\n694\t            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n695\t            25.0,\n696\t            0.0,\n697\t            \"+25pp\"\n698\t          ],\n699\t          [\n700\t            \"Qwen3-7B\",\n701\t            38.0,\n702\t            5.0,\n703\t            \"+33pp\"\n704\t          ]\n705\t        ]\n706\t      }\n707\t    ],\n708\t    \"figures\": [],\n709\t    \"analysis\": \"如果budget允许，这是worst档paper最能silence reviewer的实验。7B result (38% vs 5%) is more impressive than 1.7B result (25% vs 0%)。Combined message: 'the training methodology enables the model capacity to be utilized; without it, even larger models fail'。论文可能需要重新定位：如果7B reaches 38%，接近40% threshold，paper的overall strength significantly improves even under worst-tier 1.7B results。\\n\\n7B model有更高的capability ceiling，episode-level可能达38%（接近40% threshold但仍在worst档范围内——worst档是关于1.7B的performance，7B naturally higher）。Step-independent 7B同样collapse at step 5 (5% max)，确认credit assignment问题is model-size independent。7B的38% vs 1.7B的25%（+13pp）部分validates 'model capacity is separate bottleneck' argument。但192 GPU hours + cloud rental成本高。在worst档下，如果budget tight，这是high-value但high-cost experiment。如果run，结果强力支持narrative：'episode-level advantage holds across scales; larger models achieve higher ceiling但step-independent依然fails regardless of scale'。\"\n710\t  },\n711\t  {\n712\t    \"name\": \"Per-task-type breakdown analysis\",\n713\t    \"description\": \"Breakdown by ALFWorld task type. Shows within-environment diversity。\",\n714\t    \"results\": {\n715\t      \"pick_success_episode_level\": 30.0,\n716\t      \"pick_success_step_independent\": 0.0,\n717\t      \"clean_success_episode_level\": 20.0,\n718\t      \"clean_success_step_independent\": 0.0,\n719\t      \"heat_success_episode_level\": 25.0,\n720\t      \"heat_success_step_independent\": 0.0,\n721\t      \"cool_success_episode_level\": 35.0,\n722\t      \"cool_success_step_independent\": 5.0,\n723\t      \"examine_success_episode_level\": 10.0,\n724\t      \"examine_success_step_independent\": 0.0,\n725\t      \"pick_two_success_episode_level\": 5.0,\n726\t      \"pick_two_success_step_independent\": 0.0,\n727\t      \"episode_length_success_correlation\": -0.42,\n728\t      \"short_task_advantage\": \"cool/heat (fewer steps) have higher success\"\n729\t    },\n730\t    \"tables\": [\n731\t      {\n732\t        \"name\": \"Table: Per-task breakdown\",\n733\t        \"columns\": [\n734\t          \"Task Type\",\n735\t          \"Avg Episode Length\",\n736\t          \"Episode-Level(%)\",\n737\t          \"Step-Independent(%)\",\n738\t          \"N (val)\"\n739\t        ],\n740\t        \"rows\": [\n741\t          [\n742\t            \"pick\",\n743\t            45,\n744\t            30.0,\n745\t            0.0,\n746\t            4\n747\t          ],\n748\t          [\n749\t            \"clean\",\n750\t            48,\n751\t            20.0,\n752\t            0.0,\n753\t            3\n754\t          ],\n755\t          [\n756\t            \"heat\",\n757\t            35,\n758\t            25.0,\n759\t            0.0,\n760\t            3\n761\t          ],\n762\t          [\n763\t            \"cool\",\n764\t            30,\n765\t            35.0,\n766\t            5.0,\n767\t            3\n768\t          ],\n769\t          [\n770\t            \"examine\",\n771\t            50,\n772\t            10.0,\n773\t            0.0,\n774\t            2\n775\t          ],\n776\t          [\n777\t            \"pick_two\",\n778\t            55,\n779\t            5.0,\n780\t            0.0,\n781\t            1\n782\t          ]\n783\t        ]\n784\t      }\n785\t    ],\n786\t    \"figures\": [],\n787\t    \"analysis\": \"Small N per task type (1-4 episodes in val set) makes individual percentages unreliable，但overall trend (shorter tasks → higher success) supports mechanistic story。In worst档paper，include as supplementary analysis showing the method's advantage is consistent across task types despite varying magnitude。The length-success correlation adds another data point for the credit assignment narrative。\\n\\n在worst档下，per-task breakdown reveals episode-level advantage is universal但magnitude varies by task complexity。Shorter tasks (cool: ~30 steps, heat: ~35 steps) reach higher success (35%, 25%) because credit assignment even under h=full works better when T is smaller (gamma^0=1 for last step matters more when T smaller)。Longer tasks (examine: ~50 steps, pick_two: ~55 steps) have lower success (10%, 5%) — model capacity ceiling hits harder when trajectory is longer。Correlation r=-0.42 between episode length and success confirms mechanistic explanation。Step-independent fails uniformly across all types (0-5%), confirming the training failure is systematic not task-specific。\"\n788\t  }\n789\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ebe00c9-3b64-47d2-a443-4179165be407","uuid":"645fbca1-d8dd-4729-8d45-c704342a5e4e","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:12:43.096Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T235255/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Context window h-sweep ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"Sweep h={1,2,3,5,8,10,15,20,full} on same GRPO config. Paper核心Figure。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"h1_success_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"h2_success_rate\": 2.0,\n      \"h3_success_rate\": 4.5,\n      \"h5_success_rate\": 8.0,\n      \"h8_success_rate\": 14.0,\n      \"h10_success_rate\": 18.0,\n      \"h15_success_rate\": 22.0,\n      \"h20_success_rate\": 24.0,\n      \"h_full_success_rate\": 25.0,\n      \"cliff_threshold_h\": 5,\n      \"h1_collapse_rate\": 1.0,\n      \"h2_collapse_rate\": 0.85,\n      \"h5_action_is_valid\": 72.0,\n      \"h10_action_is_valid\": 82.0,\n      \"h_full_action_is_valid\": 88.0,\n      \"convergence_speed_h10_steps\": 15,\n      \"convergence_speed_h_full_steps\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: h-sweep results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"h\",\n          \"success_rate(%)\",\n          \"action_is_valid(%)\",\n          \"convergence_step\",\n          \"effective_discount_gamma^(T-h)_mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            0.0,\n            45.0,\n            \"N/A (collapse)\",\n            0.0001\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            2.0,\n            58.0,\n            \"N/A (near-collapse)\",\n            0.0008\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            4.5,\n            65.0,\n            20,\n            0.005\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            8.0,\n            72.0,\n            15,\n            0.03\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            14.0,\n            79.0,\n            12,\n            0.12\n          ],\n          [\n            10,\n            18.0,\n            82.0,\n            12,\n            0.22\n          ],\n          [\n            15,\n            22.0,\n            85.0,\n            10,\n            0.48\n          ],\n          [\n            20,\n            24.0,\n            87.0,\n            8,\n            0.67\n          ],\n          [\n            \"full\",\n            25.0,\n            88.0,\n            8,\n            1.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"h-sweep是worst档下paper最有价值的contribution。虽然绝对性能低，但趋势清晰：step-independent（h=1-2）catastrophically fails，episode-level（h=full）works。问题在于h=10已达full性能的72%（18/25），reviewer会argue full episode context非必要。Defense需要：(1)强调h=10在更长episode task上可能不够，(2)展示h=full的convergence speed优势，(3)argue 'full是最简方案，无需tune h'。Single seed数据使得intermediate h values的ordering可能有noise。\\n\\n在worst档位下，h-sweep仍能展示episode-level vs step-independent的gap，但曲线形态偏向gradual degradation而非sharp cliff。h=5以下gamma^(T-h)衰减到<1%导致几乎无学习信号，但h=10到h=full之间差距不大（18%→25%），削弱了'episode-level is critical'的论证力度——reviewer会argue h=10 already sufficient。绝对性能ceiling在25%使得整条曲线都不impressive。cliff在h=5左右，比hypothesis的h=10低，意味着credit assignment threshold比预期更宽松，但也说明即便给了足够context（h≥10），1.7B model的能力ceiling也只有20-25%。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-seed replication (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"2 additional seeds for episode-level config. Report mean ± std。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_success_rate\": 25.0,\n      \"seed2_success_rate\": 18.0,\n      \"seed3_success_rate\": 30.0,\n      \"mean_success_rate\": 24.3,\n      \"std_success_rate\": 6.0,\n      \"seed1_convergence_step\": 8,\n      \"seed2_convergence_step\": 15,\n      \"seed3_convergence_step\": 6,\n      \"seed1_action_is_valid\": 88.0,\n      \"seed2_action_is_valid\": 82.0,\n      \"seed3_action_is_valid\": 90.0,\n      \"mean_action_is_valid\": 86.7,\n      \"std_action_is_valid\": 4.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Multi-seed episode-level results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Seed\",\n          \"Success Rate(%)\",\n          \"Action Valid(%)\",\n          \"Convergence Step\",\n          \"Final KL\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            42,\n            25.0,\n            88.0,\n            8,\n            0.048\n          ],\n          [\n            123,\n            18.0,\n            82.0,\n            15,\n            0.092\n          ],\n          [\n            7,\n            30.0,\n            90.0,\n            6,\n            0.035\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean±Std\",\n            \"24.3±6.0\",\n            \"86.7±4.2\",\n            \"9.7±4.7\",\n            \"0.058±0.030\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Std=6pp略好于worst档定义的8-12pp下界，但仍然problematic。N=3 seeds给出的confidence interval很宽（24.3±6.0意味着95% CI约为[12, 37]），reviewer会正确指出这不够。理想需要5+ seeds但GPU budget不允许。Defense策略：(1)承认limitation，(2)强调所有seeds都远超step-independent baseline 0%，(3)variance主要在收敛speed而非final direction。\\n\\nWorst档定义multi-seed std>8pp，但我预测实际std在6-9pp范围——足以让reviewer质疑但不至于完全破坏结论。三个seed中一个会表现较差（18%），一个中等（25%，复现原始结果），一个稍好（30%）。这个variance部分来自ALFWorld task sampling的随机性（val set只有16 episodes），部分来自GRPO的inherent instability（高grad_norm, KL spikes在不同seed上timing不同）。1.7B模型的parameter space小，不同random init导致loss landscape上收敛到不同local optima。Mean 24.3%仍远超step-independent baseline（0-6%），但confidence interval宽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Credit assignment mechanism analysis (paper Figure 2)\",\n    \"description\": \"计算并可视化gamma^(T-h) effective discount, gradient signal strength, episode length correlation。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gamma_value_used\": 0.99,\n      \"mean_episode_length_T\": 48,\n      \"gamma_T_minus_1\": 0.0061,\n      \"gamma_T_minus_2\": 0.0062,\n      \"gamma_T_minus_5\": 0.0065,\n      \"gamma_T_minus_10\": 0.0068,\n      \"gamma_T_minus_20\": 0.0075,\n      \"gamma_T_minus_full\": 1.0,\n      \"gradient_signal_h1_relative\": 0.006,\n      \"gradient_signal_h5_relative\": 0.03,\n      \"gradient_signal_h10_relative\": 0.22,\n      \"gradient_signal_full_relative\": 1.0,\n      \"episode_length_success_correlation\": -0.35,\n      \"long_episode_success_drop_under_h5\": 95\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Effective discount factor analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"h\",\n          \"Mean gamma^(T-h)\",\n          \"Relative Gradient Signal\",\n          \"Observed Success(%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            0.006,\n            \"0.6%\",\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            0.012,\n            \"1.2%\",\n            2.0\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            0.03,\n            \"3.0%\",\n            8.0\n          ],\n          [\n            10,\n            0.22,\n            \"22%\",\n            18.0\n          ],\n          [\n            20,\n            0.67,\n            \"67%\",\n            24.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"full\",\n            1.0,\n            \"100%\",\n            25.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是worst档下最强的contribution piece。数学关系清晰，可视化compelling。关键insight：在RAGEN等现有工作中，默认h=1（step-independent），对应gradient signal仅0.6%——解释了为什么这些方法在long-horizon tasks上struggle。但需要小心措辞：不能overclaim 'episode-level solves multi-turn RL'（因为25%不算solved），只能claim 'episode-level is necessary first step, removing a fundamental training bottleneck'。\\n\\nMechanistic analysis本身是deterministic计算（给定gamma和episode length分布），不受worst档位的performance ceiling影响。ALFWorld平均episode length~48 steps，所以gamma^47≈0.006（h=1时first action的discount）。这个数学事实不变。但worst档下的complication是：即使h=full（gradient signal=1.0），模型也只达25%——说明gradient signal是necessary但非sufficient condition。Reviewer会argue：'你解决了gradient signal问题，但模型仍然不行，说明bottleneck在elsewhere'。需要explicitly address这一点：承认model capacity是另一个bottleneck，但credit assignment是第一个需解决的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Action-change statistics from always-on runs\",\n    \"description\": \"从exp029 checkpoints收集action-change统计：confirmatory rate, correlation with success, per-task breakdown。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_verification_episodes\": 48,\n      \"action_change_rate\": 0.35,\n      \"confirmatory_rate\": 0.65,\n      \"action_change_success_correlation_r\": 0.15,\n      \"action_change_success_correlation_p\": 0.18,\n      \"per_task_confirmatory_rate_put\": 0.72,\n      \"per_task_confirmatory_rate_clean\": 0.6,\n      \"per_task_confirmatory_rate_heat\": 0.55,\n      \"per_task_confirmatory_rate_cool\": 0.58,\n      \"per_task_confirmatory_rate_examine\": 0.7,\n      \"action_change_leads_to_success_rate\": 0.22,\n      \"no_change_leads_to_success_rate\": 0.18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Action-change statistics\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\",\n          \"95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Confirmatory rate (no action change)\",\n            \"65%\",\n            \"[52%, 78%]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Action change rate\",\n            \"35%\",\n            \"[22%, 48%]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Correlation (action_change, success)\",\n            \"r=0.15\",\n            \"p=0.18\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Success | action_change\",\n            \"22%\",\n            \"[10%, 34%]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Success | no_change\",\n            \"18%\",\n            \"[8%, 28%]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"统计结果不支持action-change作为meaningful reward signal。Correlation not significant，delta too small，CI too wide。这组数据是worst档叙事转向的empirical justification：不是我们选择不做selective verification，而是数据显示在当前performance level下selective verification lacks statistical grounding。Paper中可以brief mention作为'future work when base agent is stronger'。\\n\\n在worst档下，episode-level model只有25% success rate，导致action-change统计的样本量极小且noisy。Confirmatory rate 65%落在worst档定义的50-70%范围内，但correlation with success仅r=0.15（p=0.18, not significant）。这是因为：(1)成功episodes太少（~12/48），统计power不足；(2)25%的模型经常在错误轨道上，verification后的action change可能是从一个错误action换到另一个错误action，而非corrective。Action change→success rate (22%) vs no change→success rate (18%)的delta仅4pp，远不够支撑'action change is informative signal'的claim。这直接explains为什么在worst档下必须放弃selective verification story。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Selective verification implementation\",\n    \"description\": \"实现binary verify/skip decision。Code-only, no GPU。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"implementation_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"code_lines_added\": 350,\n      \"integration_test_pass\": true,\n      \"note\": \"implementation ready but not deployed for training due to plan_005 results\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"在worst档叙事下，这个实验stop at implementation。Paper中不报告selective verification training results，而是在discussion section brief mention implementation exists but 'requires stronger base agent to provide meaningful training signal'。\\n\\nImplementation本身是engineering work，不受worst档影响。代码可以完成，但基于plan_005的统计结果（action-change correlation not significant），decision是不proceed to training。代码保留为future work artifact。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"B-IAVR selective verification training\",\n    \"description\": \"Train selective verification policy via episode-level GRPO。在worst档下执行但预期效果不佳。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"training_status\": \"completed_but_ineffective\",\n      \"final_success_rate\": 18.0,\n      \"always_on_baseline_success\": 25.0,\n      \"success_delta_vs_always_on\": -7.0,\n      \"verification_rate_reduction\": 12.0,\n      \"cost_reduction_pct\": 8.0,\n      \"training_stability\": \"unstable\",\n      \"convergence_step\": \"no clear convergence\",\n      \"reward_signal_noise\": \"high\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: B-IAVR training outcome\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Config\",\n          \"Success(%)\",\n          \"Verify Rate(%)\",\n          \"Cost Reduction(%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Always-on (baseline)\",\n            25.0,\n            100,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B-IAVR (trained)\",\n            18.0,\n            88,\n            8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Delta\",\n            -7.0,\n            -12,\n            \"+8\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"结果confirms worst档prediction：selective verification在base agent只有25%时无法有意义地训练。-7pp success drop换取仅8% cost reduction，Pareto-dominated by always-on。Paper中不报告此结果，或仅作为negative result brief mention to motivate 'stronger base agent needed'。\\n\\nWorst档定义selective_verification_rate_reduction在0-15%，selective_vs_always_on_success_delta在8-15pp。模型从25% base开始，加入verify/skip decision后引入额外exploration space，但base performance本身就marginal。Agent在只有25% success的情况下，缺乏足够的positive reward signal来学习WHEN to verify——大部分trajectory都是failure，无论verify还是skip。结果是verification rate仅下降12%（几乎always verify因为policy没学到有用的skip pattern），且success下降7pp（从25%到18%）因为额外decision point增加了policy complexity。这不构成meaningful contribution。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Selective verification full comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Compare always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"always_on_success\": 25.0,\n      \"always_on_verify_rate\": 100,\n      \"biavr_success\": 18.0,\n      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 88,\n      \"no_verify_success\": 15.0,\n      \"no_verify_verify_rate\": 0,\n      \"random_p50_success\": 20.0,\n      \"random_p50_verify_rate\": 50,\n      \"confidence_threshold_success\": 21.0,\n      \"confidence_threshold_verify_rate\": 65\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Full comparison (NOT included in worst-tier paper)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Success(%)\",\n          \"Verify Rate(%)\",\n          \"Tokens/Episode\",\n          \"Cost Reduction(%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Always-on\",\n            25.0,\n            100,\n            4800,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B-IAVR (ours)\",\n            18.0,\n            88,\n            4420,\n            8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"No-verify\",\n            15.0,\n            0,\n            2400,\n            50\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random-p=0.5\",\n            20.0,\n            50,\n            3600,\n            25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Confidence-threshold\",\n            21.0,\n            65,\n            3900,\n            19\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"This entire comparison suite becomes 'data we collected but don't include in paper'。B-IAVR被simpler baselines dominate是fatal for selective verification claim。在worst档pure methodology paper中，这组数据的唯一价值是supporting the narrative 'future work: once episode-level training achieves higher ceiling, selective verification becomes viable'。\\n\\n在25% ceiling下，所有selective methods都worse than always-on。Random-p=0.5 (20%) actually competitive with trained B-IAVR (18%)——trained policy没有学到比random更好的策略，这是devastating negative result。Confidence-threshold (21%) slightly better因为它是heuristic rule而非learned，less prone to policy degradation。整个comparison suite展示：在low-performance regime下，verification的选择性本身不是bottleneck，base capability才是。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"No-verify ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level GRPO without self-verification。Lower bound实验。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"success_rate\": 15.0,\n      \"action_is_valid\": 78.0,\n      \"delta_vs_always_on\": -10.0,\n      \"mean_episode_length\": 38,\n      \"convergence_step\": 10\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Verification value\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Config\",\n          \"Success(%)\",\n          \"Action Valid(%)\",\n          \"Avg Steps\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Episode-level + verification\",\n            25.0,\n            88.0,\n            48\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Episode-level, no verification\",\n            15.0,\n            78.0,\n            38\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Step-independent + verification\",\n            0.0,\n            65.0,\n            50\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"三行对比table实际很有说服力：step-independent完全fails无论有无verification，episode-level without verification仍有15%。Message: training methodology是前提条件，verification是锦上添花。这fit worst档pure methodology paper的narrative。\\n\\n移除verification后，agent失去每步的self-correction机会。从25%降到15%，delta=10pp。这在worst档下actually是有用的数据点——证明verification本身有10pp价值。但这个delta不够dramatic来支撑'selective verification is the key innovation'的story。在pure methodology paper中可以brief report作为：'verification contributes +10pp, confirming its utility, but our focus is on the training methodology that enables ANY multi-turn RL to work'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Stratify action-change correlation by policy entropy, test partial correlation。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_correlation_r\": 0.15,\n      \"overall_p\": 0.18,\n      \"low_entropy_stratum_r\": 0.08,\n      \"low_entropy_stratum_p\": 0.55,\n      \"high_entropy_stratum_r\": 0.2,\n      \"high_entropy_stratum_p\": 0.22,\n      \"partial_correlation_controlling_entropy\": 0.12,\n      \"partial_correlation_p\": 0.28,\n      \"n_episodes_per_stratum\": 24\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"在worst档下这组分析的结论是negative：无法reject null hypothesis (action-change = noise)。Paper中不report，或在appendix作为'limitation: at current performance level, insufficient statistical power to establish action-change as reliable signal'。\\n\\n在worst档25% success下，整体correlation已not significant (r=0.15, p=0.18)。Stratify by entropy后每层只有~24 episodes，statistical power进一步削弱。Low entropy stratum（policy confident）中action-change很少发生（agent已committed to action），correlation near zero。High entropy stratum中有more action-change但也more randomness，correlation略高但仍not significant。Partial correlation r=0.12 (p=0.28)完全不支持'action-change is signal not noise'的claim。根本原因：样本量太小 + base performance太低导致signal-to-noise ratio极差。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes\",\n    \"description\": \"Inject random action changes vs verification-triggered. Compare success。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"verification_triggered_success\": 22.0,\n      \"random_change_success\": 16.0,\n      \"no_change_baseline_success\": 18.0,\n      \"delta_triggered_vs_random\": 6.0,\n      \"delta_triggered_vs_random_p\": 0.25,\n      \"n_episodes\": 48\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Causal intervention (insufficient power)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"Success(%)\",\n          \"N\",\n          \"95% CI\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Verification-triggered change\",\n            22.0,\n            48,\n            \"[11%, 33%]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random change (same rate)\",\n            16.0,\n            48,\n            \"[6%, 26%]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"No change control\",\n            18.0,\n            48,\n            \"[8%, 28%]\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CIs完全overlap。Experiment was run but results inconclusive。在pure methodology paper中不report。File under 'more data needed at higher performance level'。\\n\\nVerification-triggered changes (22%) vs random changes (16%) shows 6pp gap，方向正确但p=0.25 not significant。N=48 episodes不够detect这个effect size。No-change baseline (18%)介于两者之间，使得interpretation模糊：triggered changes可能beneficial，但也可能just noise given wide CIs。在25% performance regime下，即使verification IS informative，effect size太小to detect reliably。另一个confounder：random changes有时accidentally correct（16% vs no-change 18%只差2pp），suggesting verification的causal contribution marginal。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\",\n    \"description\": \"Train B-IAVR with different reward signals: action-change, random, confidence-based。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"action_change_reward_success\": 18.0,\n      \"action_change_reward_verify_rate\": 88,\n      \"random_reward_success\": 17.0,\n      \"random_reward_verify_rate\": 82,\n      \"confidence_reward_success\": 19.0,\n      \"confidence_reward_verify_rate\": 85,\n      \"all_configs_worse_than_always_on\": true,\n      \"best_reward_signal\": \"confidence (marginal)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Reward ablation (NOT in paper)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Reward Signal\",\n          \"Success(%)\",\n          \"Verify Rate(%)\",\n          \"vs Always-on Delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Action-change (ours)\",\n            18.0,\n            88,\n            -7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random trigger\",\n            17.0,\n            82,\n            -8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Confidence-based\",\n            19.0,\n            85,\n            -6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Always-on (no selection)\",\n            25.0,\n            100,\n            0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"192 GPU hours for a negative result。在worst档下，建议NOT run此实验——plan_007的negative result已sufficient to abandon selective verification direction。Save GPU budget for more h-sweep seeds or ScienceWorld transfer。\\n\\n所有reward signals在25% base下都无法学到meaningful selective policy。Action-change reward (18%, verify 88%) vs random reward (17%, verify 82%)的差距仅1pp success——action-change没有demonstrable advantage over random。Confidence-based reward margionally better (19%) because它at least correlates with model's own uncertainty（哪怕calibration差）。但关键point：所有trained selective policies都worse than always-on (25%)。Reward signal choice irrelevant when base performance insufficient to generate learning signal。192 GPU hours换来的结论是'all approaches fail equally in low-performance regime'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ARES reproduction + comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ares_success\": 20.0,\n      \"ares_verify_rate\": 60,\n      \"ares_cost_reduction\": 30,\n      \"biavr_success\": 18.0,\n      \"biavr_verify_rate\": 88,\n      \"biavr_cost_reduction\": 8,\n      \"ares_dominates_biavr\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: ARES comparison (NOT in paper)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Success(%)\",\n          \"Verify Rate(%)\",\n          \"Cost Red.(%)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Always-on\",\n            25.0,\n            100,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARES (SFT router)\",\n            20.0,\n            60,\n            30\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B-IAVR (ours, RL)\",\n            18.0,\n            88,\n            8\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ARES dominates B-IAVR on Pareto frontier。但在worst档pure methodology paper中，这个comparison不needed也不helpful。如果include，只会invite reviewer质疑'why not just use SFT'。建议NOT run，节省24 GPU hours。\\n\\nARES使用SFT（supervised从expert demonstrations学）which is more data-efficient than RL in low-performance regime。SFT router可以直接学human-pattern的'when to verify'而不依赖agent自身的exploration。预测ARES achieves 20% success at 60% verify rate，Pareto-dominating B-IAVR (18% at 88% verify rate)。这是because SFT不需要agent自己产生positive signal——它从expert data中学。Devastating for our RL-based approach，但irrelevant for worst档paper because we abandon selective verification entirely。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ScienceWorld transfer (episode-level advantage)\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld。Second environment for generalization。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"episode_level_success\": 15.0,\n      \"step_independent_success\": 2.0,\n      \"episode_level_action_is_valid\": 75.0,\n      \"step_independent_action_is_valid\": 55.0,\n      \"episode_level_convergence_step\": 12,\n      \"step_independent_collapse_step\": 4,\n      \"mean_episode_length_scienceworld\": 35\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cross-environment validation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Environment\",\n          \"Episode-Level(%)\",\n          \"Step-Independent(%)\",\n          \"Ratio\",\n          \"Mean Episode Length\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"ALFWorld\",\n            25.0,\n            0.0,\n            \"∞ (0→25)\",\n            48\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ScienceWorld\",\n            15.0,\n            2.0,\n            \"7.5x\",\n            35\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-environment result是worst档paper的第二大contribution。Pattern consistent across environments strongly支持mechanistic explanation。Reviewer concern #2 (single env) addressed。72 GPU hours well-spent for worst档narrative。绝对值低但ratio large，且collapse pattern identical——这是methodology insight的generalization evidence。\\n\\nScienceWorld比ALFWorld更难（state space更大，natural language更复杂），1.7B model的absolute performance会更低。Episode-level仍展示优势（15% vs 2%），倍率~7.5x（高于ALFWorld的~4x因为ScienceWorld的longer episodes使credit assignment问题更severe）。Step-independent在step 4 collapse（与ALFWorld pattern一致）。绝对数字15%不impressive，但cross-environment consistency是powerful evidence for the mechanism。在worst档pure methodology paper中，这是ADDRESS single-environment concern的关键实验。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"7B model scaling verification\",\n    \"description\": \"Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B。Address model size concern。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"episode_level_7b_success\": 38.0,\n      \"step_independent_7b_success\": 5.0,\n      \"episode_level_7b_action_is_valid\": 92.0,\n      \"step_independent_7b_collapse_step\": 5,\n      \"episode_level_7b_convergence_step\": 6,\n      \"delta_7b_vs_1_7b_episode_level\": 13\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Model scaling\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Episode-Level(%)\",\n          \"Step-Independent(%)\",\n          \"Advantage\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-1.7B\",\n            25.0,\n            0.0,\n            \"+25pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-7B\",\n            38.0,\n            5.0,\n            \"+33pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"如果budget允许，这是worst档paper最能silence reviewer的实验。7B result (38% vs 5%) is more impressive than 1.7B result (25% vs 0%)。Combined message: 'the training methodology enables the model capacity to be utilized; without it, even larger models fail'。论文可能需要重新定位：如果7B reaches 38%，接近40% threshold，paper的overall strength significantly improves even under worst-tier 1.7B results。\\n\\n7B model有更高的capability ceiling，episode-level可能达38%（接近40% threshold但仍在worst档范围内——worst档是关于1.7B的performance，7B naturally higher）。Step-independent 7B同样collapse at step 5 (5% max)，确认credit assignment问题is model-size independent。7B的38% vs 1.7B的25%（+13pp）部分validates 'model capacity is separate bottleneck' argument。但192 GPU hours + cloud rental成本高。在worst档下，如果budget tight，这是high-value但high-cost experiment。如果run，结果强力支持narrative：'episode-level advantage holds across scales; larger models achieve higher ceiling但step-independent依然fails regardless of scale'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-task-type breakdown analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Breakdown by ALFWorld task type. Shows within-environment diversity。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"pick_success_episode_level\": 30.0,\n      \"pick_success_step_independent\": 0.0,\n      \"clean_success_episode_level\": 20.0,\n      \"clean_success_step_independent\": 0.0,\n      \"heat_success_episode_level\": 25.0,\n      \"heat_success_step_independent\": 0.0,\n      \"cool_success_episode_level\": 35.0,\n      \"cool_success_step_independent\": 5.0,\n      \"examine_success_episode_level\": 10.0,\n      \"examine_success_step_independent\": 0.0,\n      \"pick_two_success_episode_level\": 5.0,\n      \"pick_two_success_step_independent\": 0.0,\n      \"episode_length_success_correlation\": -0.42,\n      \"short_task_advantage\": \"cool/heat (fewer steps) have higher success\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Per-task breakdown\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Task Type\",\n          \"Avg Episode Length\",\n          \"Episode-Level(%)\",\n          \"Step-Independent(%)\",\n          \"N (val)\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"pick\",\n            45,\n            30.0,\n            0.0,\n            4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"clean\",\n            48,\n            20.0,\n            0.0,\n            3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"heat\",\n            35,\n            25.0,\n            0.0,\n            3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cool\",\n            30,\n            35.0,\n            5.0,\n            3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"examine\",\n            50,\n            10.0,\n            0.0,\n            2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"pick_two\",\n            55,\n            5.0,\n            0.0,\n            1\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Small N per task type (1-4 episodes in val set) makes individual percentages unreliable，但overall trend (shorter tasks → higher success) supports mechanistic story。In worst档paper，include as supplementary analysis showing the method's advantage is consistent across task types despite varying magnitude。The length-success correlation adds another data point for the credit assignment narrative。\\n\\n在worst档下，per-task breakdown reveals episode-level advantage is universal但magnitude varies by task complexity。Shorter tasks (cool: ~30 steps, heat: ~35 steps) reach higher success (35%, 25%) because credit assignment even under h=full works better when T is smaller (gamma^0=1 for last step matters more when T smaller)。Longer tasks (examine: ~50 steps, pick_two: ~55 steps) have lower success (10%, 5%) — model capacity ceiling hits harder when trajectory is longer。Correlation r=-0.42 between episode length and success confirms mechanistic explanation。Step-independent fails uniformly across all types (0-5%), confirming the training failure is systematic not task-specific。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":789,"startLine":1,"totalLines":789}}}
